---
// WRITTEN FROM SCRATCH against what this site actually does.
//
// Do NOT replace this with a boilerplate policy pulled from another company.
// A borrowed Terms/Privacy pair belonging to "Uppit AI LLC" was considered for
// this page and rejected: it was someone else's copyrighted text, and it
// described SMS opt-in flows, form fields including budget range, cookies,
// pixels and analytics vendors, none of which exist here. A privacy policy is
// a legal representation. Claiming to collect data you do not collect is its
// own kind of false statement.
//
// UPDATED 2026-08-21: the site gained its first form -- the SMS opt-in at
// /text-me -- and this file changed in the same commit, as the note below
// required. The "no contact forms" claim was removed because it became false.
//
// If the site gains ANOTHER form, analytics, or a newsletter, THIS FILE MUST
// CHANGE IN THE SAME COMMIT. The SMS section is also a carrier compliance
// artefact: the 10DLC campaign cites this policy, and carriers require that it
// forbid sharing opt-in data with third parties. Do not weaken that paragraph.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  kicker="Short, because this website collects almost nothing."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website has <strong>no analytics, no cookies, and no tracking of any
    kind</strong>. We do not build a profile of you, we do not sell or rent
    information about you, and there is no advertising network involved in any
    part of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is <strong>exactly one form</strong> on this site: the
    <a href="/text-me">text me the demo</a> page, where you can ask us to send
    you a recording by SMS. It is the only place we collect anything, it is
    entirely optional, and what happens to that information is described in
    full below.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing at all, unless you fill in the SMS opt-in form. We set no cookies
    and run no analytics or tracking scripts.
  </p>
  <p>
    One honest caveat: like any website, this one is served by a hosting
    provider, and that provider automatically records standard technical
    request information such as IP address, browser type, and which page was
    requested. That is a normal function of serving a web page and of keeping
    the service running and secure. We do not use those logs to identify or
    profile visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Text messages, and what we do with your number</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit the form on the <a href="/text-me">text me the demo</a> page,
    you are giving us express written consent to send you text messages about
    the demo you asked for and follow-up about that service.
    <strong>Message frequency may vary.</strong>
    <strong>Standard message and data rates may apply.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Consent to receive text messages is <strong>not a condition of any
    purchase</strong>. The checkbox is never pre-ticked, and SMS consent is
    asked for separately from anything else.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>To stop receiving messages, reply STOP to any message.</strong> That
    removes your number permanently and automatically, and we check that
    suppression list at the moment of sending rather than when a batch is built,
    so an opt-out always takes effect. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help, or
    email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you submit the form we record your name, business name, phone number,
    the date and time, your IP address, and the exact version of the consent
    wording shown to you. We keep that record so we can demonstrate, if a
    carrier or regulator ever asks, that you agreed and what you agreed to.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not sell, rent, share, or otherwise disclose your mobile
    number or your SMS consent to any third party for their marketing
    purposes</strong>, and no third party receives it for any purpose other
    than delivering the message you asked for. Messages are delivered through
    our telephony provider, who transmits them on our behalf and is not
    permitted to use your number for anything else.
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Contact happens through LinkedIn or email. If you message us, we receive
    whatever you choose to send: your name, your email address, and whatever
    you write. We use it to reply to you and to discuss potential work. Nothing
    more.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those conversations sit on LinkedIn's and your email provider's systems, and
    their privacy policies apply to them, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>The Client Optimal LinkedIn application</h2>
  <p>
    Client Optimal operates a private LinkedIn application used to publish posts
    to <strong>its own founder's LinkedIn account</strong>. It signs in through
    LinkedIn OAuth, which gives it that account's own profile identifier and
    permission to post as that account. It uses them for nothing else.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application <strong>does not read, collect, or store data about any other
    LinkedIn member</strong>. It does not access your profile, your connections,
    your feed, or your activity. It does not scrape LinkedIn, and it takes no
    automated action on anyone else's posts. It is private to Client Optimal and
    is not offered to anyone else.
  </p>
  <p>
    Running it involves a small number of service providers: the access token and
    the queued posts are held in the automation platform that runs the workflow,
    the drafts are generated by an AI provider, and approvals are sent through a
    messaging service. They process that information only to operate the
    workflow, on our instructions. None of it is sold, rented, or used for
    advertising, and none of it concerns visitors to this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Separately, we sometimes write a reply to someone's public post by hand. Where
    we use our own tools to help draft one, the post is something we supplied
    manually, it is used only to prepare that reply, and we do not build or keep a
    profile of the person who wrote it. The reply is always reviewed and posted by
    a person.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information. We do not share it for
    anyone else's marketing purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    For <strong>this website</strong>, the only third parties involved are the
    infrastructure providers that host it and route its domain, and they only ever
    see the standard technical request information described above. The separate
    set of providers used to run our LinkedIn posting workflow is described in the
    section above, and none of them receive anything about visitors to this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep correspondence for as long as it is useful to the conversation or
    the working relationship, and delete it when it is not. Hosting logs are
    retained by the hosting provider under their own retention schedule.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Since we collect nothing on the website itself, there is no account to
    close, no profile to correct, and no mailing list to leave. If you have
    emailed or messaged us and want that correspondence deleted, ask and we
    will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is for business audiences and is not directed at children
    under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this website changes in a way that affects privacy, for example by adding
    a contact form or analytics, this page will be updated at the same time and
    the effective date above will change.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can go to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>{' '}
    or via <a href={contact.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
